            <ArticleTitle>Intraoperative cardiac arrest in a neurosurgical patient: what are the options?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intraoperative cardiac arrest is uncommon. We describe a case of intraoperative cardiac arrest in a patient undergoing anesthesia for surgical repair of an intracranial arteriovenous malformation (AVM).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
